WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.916
<i>The license plate matches</i>
<i>a stolen vehicle report.</i>

2
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.583
<i>The car is stolen.</i>
<i>I repeat. the car is stolen.</i>

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

4
00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:35.708
Stop!

5
00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:16.708
Step out of the car
with your hands in the air!

6
00:01:21.083 --> 00:01:22.500
So what do we do now?

7
00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:25.750
This is your last warning!
Step out of the car!

8
00:01:27.791 --> 00:01:29.916
We let both cars
reach the middle of the bridge.

9
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.000
What?

10
00:01:41.916 --> 00:01:43.833
You're crazy!

11
00:01:45.708 --> 00:01:48.083
- They'll back down.
- Why would they back down?

12
00:01:48.166 --> 00:01:50.666
- Stop the vehicle immediately!
- Because I'm not gonna.

13
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.166
Stop the car. right now!

14
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:11.041
Now they have to turn around.
And those extra seconds will be precious.

15
00:02:11.708 --> 00:02:14.333
Unbelievable!
And I thought <i>I </i>was the crazy one.

16
00:02:14.416 --> 00:02:15.750
Clearly. <i>you're </i>the nutcase.

17
00:02:55.916 --> 00:02:58.500
How about we take a walk
in the woods under the pale moonlight?

18
00:03:00.666 --> 00:03:02.000
I'd love to.

19
00:04:03.958 --> 00:04:06.416
Don't you find
that we make a romantic couple?

20
00:04:06.916 --> 00:04:10.583
Young lovers on a yacht.
preparing a new heist…

21
00:04:10.666 --> 00:04:12.208
The perfect couple.

22
00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.583
And we even have a full moon.

23
00:04:27.875 --> 00:04:29.541
{\an8}Hey. babe. look.

24
00:04:29.625 --> 00:04:32.458
The Golden Tower is all lit up for us.

25
00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:35.166
Our first kiss was on a boat.

26
00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.625
Maybe it's a sign
we should get one and live on it.

27
00:04:37.708 --> 00:04:41.583
You know. somewhere like…
Venice or. um… Amsterdam.

28
00:04:41.666 --> 00:04:43.416
Doesn't it rain too much?

29
00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.250
All the better for us.

30
00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.000
We'll stay in bed all day.

31
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.916
C'mon. answer it.
It's your mother. She might be sick again.

32
00:05:03.083 --> 00:05:05.666
It's okay. Mom.
Don't worry. You're not bothering me.

33
00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.333
Are you okay?

34
00:05:07.416 --> 00:05:11.208
For the past 17 days.
I've been listening to those silly chimes.

35
00:05:11.291 --> 00:05:13.541
<i>Imagine how I feel.</i>

36
00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:16.916
<i>All day I keep looking at my phone.</i>
<i>hoping for a message from you.</i>

37
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.375
And when it arrives. I'm afraid to look.

38
00:05:20.291 --> 00:05:23.083
I'm afraid that it might be
your last message to me.

39
00:05:24.291 --> 00:05:27.958
<i>But then I think about how beautiful it</i>
<i>would be if you felt the same way too.</i>

40
00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.000
<i>So. I open it.</i>

41
00:05:31.375 --> 00:05:33.500
<i>"Never in my life have I felt</i>
<i>the way I did</i>

42
00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:35.625
<i>when I walked up those steps</i>
<i>to the attic with you."</i>

43
00:05:36.458 --> 00:05:39.000
When I read your message.
I ran out of my house

44
00:05:39.083 --> 00:05:40.791
<i>and didn't stop running until it was dark.</i>

45
00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:51.208
It was like a dream.

46
00:05:51.291 --> 00:05:53.833
I felt the same.

47
00:05:53.916 --> 00:05:56.958
All I wanted to do was to wait
by the door and watch you run back to me.

48
00:05:57.041 --> 00:06:00.916
hot and your shirt covered in sweat.
and me wrapped in it.

49
00:06:02.458 --> 00:06:04.708
And… as I look at the Golden Tower.

50
00:06:04.791 --> 00:06:07.875
I'm blind to its beauty
because all I can think of is you.

51
00:06:14.125 --> 00:06:15.583
I gotta go now.

52
00:06:21.583 --> 00:06:23.375
I guess you're thinking.

53
00:06:23.458 --> 00:06:27.416
"Wow. what a weird conversation
to have with your mother." Huh?

54
00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:31.625
No. you can have
whatever conversation you want.

55
00:06:39.166 --> 00:06:41.958
You don't want to ask me.
but I'm still gonna tell you.

56
00:06:42.041 --> 00:06:43.791
It's just that Bruce
decided to say goodbye

57
00:06:43.875 --> 00:06:46.083
to his past life and throw a party.

58
00:06:46.166 --> 00:06:49.375
He was saying goodbye
to partying and traveling

59
00:06:49.458 --> 00:06:52.458
and… sleeping around
with thousands of girls.

60
00:06:52.541 --> 00:06:55.666
He was saying goodbye
to the life he had before meeting me.

61
00:06:57.625 --> 00:07:01.208
And do you know
why he wanted to end all of that?

62
00:07:03.708 --> 00:07:05.875
Because he's in love with me.

63
00:07:07.916 --> 00:07:11.125
And now all he wants to do
is snuggle up on the sofa.

64
00:07:11.208 --> 00:07:14.833
watching movies
and eating popcorn together every night.

65
00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:22.750
But… I've never experienced
all these things he's grown tired of.

66
00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:28.541
Is that necessarily a bad thing?
If you're happy.

67
00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.208
I was a virgin. Roi.

68
00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:39.125
A 36-year-old virgin who had only
gotten laid through her VR headset.

69
00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:42.791
- Okay…
- Bruce is the only man I've had sex with.

70
00:07:45.041 --> 00:07:46.208
Not anymore.

71
00:07:46.291 --> 00:07:48.208
Someone new has come into my life.

72
00:07:49.125 --> 00:07:51.333
This guy has swept me off my feet.

73
00:07:56.833 --> 00:07:58.833
It's like an obsession.

74
00:08:14.625 --> 00:08:18.125
I'm sorry. I was cleaning myself up.
and I fell asleep.

75
00:08:18.208 --> 00:08:19.541
I should go.

76
00:08:19.625 --> 00:08:21.500
No. stay. I'll go. It's okay.

77
00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:25.708
Bye.

78
00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:38.666
Thank you.

79
00:08:43.166 --> 00:08:45.125
I wanted to open the door.

80
00:08:46.041 --> 00:08:47.541
Or maybe I didn't.

81
00:08:48.333 --> 00:08:50.291
<i>Ha! Do it!</i>

82
00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.791
Hey! Are you done in there?
Some of us have to pee!

83
00:09:17.875 --> 00:09:19.750
How are we gonna get out?

84
00:09:29.125 --> 00:09:31.958
It was an irrational attraction.
My brain had stopped working.

85
00:09:38.708 --> 00:09:40.666
<i>And suddenly. I didn't care anymore.</i>

86
00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:43.333
<i>I could hear all the noise.</i>
<i>the music. the voices.</i>

87
00:09:43.416 --> 00:09:46.208
<i>but above it all.</i>
<i>I could hear his heart beating.</i>

88
00:09:46.291 --> 00:09:50.916
<i>Pum-pum… Pum-pum…</i>
<i>Pounding like at a rock concert.</i>

89
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:54.000
<i>And I can't explain it. but…</i>
<i>I didn't feel guilty or scared.</i>

90
00:09:54.083 --> 00:09:55.583
<i>I just wanted to be there.</i>

91
00:09:55.666 --> 00:09:59.583
<i>Naked against his skin…</i>
<i>as he carried me through the crowd.</i>

92
00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:03.125
And I would have gone anywhere with him.

93
00:10:15.125 --> 00:10:20.291
<i>Crashing in the ocean from way above</i>

94
00:10:23.541 --> 00:10:28.125
<i>Got the music in you. baby</i>
<i>Tell me why</i>

95
00:10:28.208 --> 00:10:32.458
<i>Got the music in you. baby</i>
<i>Tell me why</i>

96
00:10:33.708 --> 00:10:40.041
<i>You've been locked in here forever</i>
<i>And you just can't say goodbye…</i>

97
00:10:41.375 --> 00:10:44.041
<i>I remember beams of light</i>
<i>streaming into the attic.</i>

98
00:10:44.625 --> 00:10:45.958
<i>Like a lighthouse.</i>

99
00:10:49.458 --> 00:10:52.291
<i>And the sound of glass chimes</i>
<i>moving in the air.</i>

100
00:10:52.375 --> 00:10:54.333
<i>I was drowning in waves of orgasms.</i>

101
00:10:54.416 --> 00:10:56.666
<i>though he begged me</i>
<i>to wait until we came at the same time.</i>

102
00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:59.083
<i>and I grabbed the carpet with my nails--</i>

103
00:10:59.166 --> 00:11:02.375
Thank you. Enough.
I get the picture. I know what you mean.

104
00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.333
Listen. Keila.

105
00:11:04.416 --> 00:11:07.041
usually. I would say
it's better to forget about it.

106
00:11:07.541 --> 00:11:09.041
It's just a fling.

107
00:11:09.541 --> 00:11:12.750
But considering
what I heard you say to your "mother."

108
00:11:13.958 --> 00:11:15.708
maybe this is something serious.

109
00:11:15.791 --> 00:11:17.958
I didn't think this would lead
to anything either.

110
00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:21.375
but then he said something
that changed everything.

111
00:11:22.458 --> 00:11:23.958
I'd really like to see you again.

112
00:11:26.041 --> 00:11:27.833
Are you good with numbers?

113
00:11:28.916 --> 00:11:30.916
I'd say it's my specialty.

114
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.458
655-347-949.

115
00:11:34.041 --> 00:11:36.166
And now his number
is tattooed inside my brain.

116
00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.166
and I'll never forget it. even if I'm old
and frail. dying with Alzheimer's.

117
00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.375
The first three days.
I managed not to text him.

118
00:11:42.458 --> 00:11:43.625
But on the fourth day…

119
00:11:43.708 --> 00:11:46.666
In the beginning. it was
just a few messages each day. but now…

120
00:11:47.333 --> 00:11:50.958
Now we text each other like 30 times a day
and maybe more.

121
00:11:51.041 --> 00:11:52.750
And once he called me in front of Bruce.

122
00:11:53.458 --> 00:11:56.416
I saved his number on my phone
as "Mom." so he's not suspicious.

123
00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:58.208
I told him that she wasn't well.

124
00:11:58.291 --> 00:12:01.041
I pretended that
she had some kinda kidney problem.

125
00:12:02.666 --> 00:12:04.541
It's driving me crazy. Roi.

126
00:12:05.041 --> 00:12:06.750
I'm in love with Bruce.
but at the same time.

127
00:12:06.833 --> 00:12:08.083
I'm hoping Claudio will call me.

128
00:12:08.166 --> 00:12:09.791
<i>And if he doesn't text me.</i>

129
00:12:09.875 --> 00:12:12.458
<i>I repeat in my head over and over again</i>
<i>the previous messages</i>

130
00:12:12.541 --> 00:12:14.208
<i>that I've learned by heart.</i>

131
00:12:15.208 --> 00:12:18.791
- <i>Are you sure you love Bruce?</i>
- <i>Yes. of course. I do.</i>

132
00:12:18.875 --> 00:12:21.958
That's why I haven't seen Claudio
since the party and why we only text.

133
00:12:24.208 --> 00:12:25.333
What?

134
00:12:25.416 --> 00:12:27.458
- It's much worse.
- What do you mean?

135
00:12:27.541 --> 00:12:30.791
Hoping that he'll text you is worse
than screwing in the bathroom.

136
00:12:31.666 --> 00:12:34.125
Keila. one-night stands
can happen to us all.

137
00:12:34.208 --> 00:12:36.666
And we get over it. and we move on.

138
00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:39.750
But spending all day
waiting for the phone to ring.

139
00:12:39.833 --> 00:12:40.833
hoping it's him.

140
00:12:40.916 --> 00:12:43.666
reading his messages.
remembering moments you've shared…

141
00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:49.458
Keila.

142
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.083
You know you're cheating on Bruce.

143
00:12:54.916 --> 00:12:57.875
You changed the guy's name to "Mom"
on your phone. That says it all.

144
00:13:00.041 --> 00:13:01.500
He deserves better.

145
00:13:09.875 --> 00:13:15.666
Rise and shine!
Sun's up! Get out of bed! A new day calls!

146
00:13:16.708 --> 00:13:19.500
Wakey. wakey. people!
No rest for the wicked!

147
00:13:19.583 --> 00:13:21.166
A new day has dawned!

148
00:13:23.833 --> 00:13:26.708
I know what you're all thinking. Mm?

149
00:13:27.208 --> 00:13:29.708
You're wondering.
why's he serving breakfast?

150
00:13:29.791 --> 00:13:31.916
Why's he still wearing yesterday's
dirty clothes?

151
00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.083
And two bullet holes in his chest.
What's with that?

152
00:13:35.166 --> 00:13:37.500
To be precise. they're not real bullets.
They're toy pellets.

153
00:13:37.583 --> 00:13:41.541
Well. let's just say
that I am currently experiencing things…

154
00:13:41.625 --> 00:13:44.000
that I have never experienced
in my life before.

155
00:13:44.083 --> 00:13:45.083
What things?

156
00:13:47.333 --> 00:13:48.791
My wallet was stolen.

157
00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:54.875
A master stroke.
an act of pure… prestidigitation.

158
00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:00.791
And then I experienced
a magical night together with this woman…

159
00:14:02.291 --> 00:14:04.416
This is the same woman who shot me.

160
00:14:05.291 --> 00:14:06.708
And it's not important!

161
00:14:06.791 --> 00:14:10.166
The woman fascinates me.
And that's what's so surprising.

162
00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:11.625
Because. Candela…

163
00:14:12.791 --> 00:14:14.166
Her name's Candela.

164
00:14:14.666 --> 00:14:18.666
…represents just about everything
I've disapproved of my entire adult life.

165
00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.083
And what are
these things you disapprove of?

166
00:14:21.166 --> 00:14:24.291
I've never had time
for these flamboyant women.

167
00:14:24.375 --> 00:14:26.958
<i>The kind that waltz into restaurants</i>
<i>like they own it.</i>

168
00:14:27.041 --> 00:14:30.750
The kind who grab you by the arm
and drag you all over the place.

169
00:14:30.833 --> 00:14:32.333
The kind that laughs out loud.

170
00:14:33.333 --> 00:14:36.416
The kind of woman
that's… constantly managing.

171
00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:37.958
<i>And organizing things.</i>

172
00:14:38.041 --> 00:14:39.583
With no table manners.

173
00:14:39.666 --> 00:14:41.583
<i>Stuffing themselves</i>
<i>like they were starving.</i>

174
00:14:41.666 --> 00:14:43.500
And had just come off a hunger strike!

175
00:14:44.541 --> 00:14:48.166
Slobbering on her fingers.
sucking and biting and licking.

176
00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:51.916
<i>And lapping up juices on her lips.</i>
<i>But today…</i>

177
00:14:53.458 --> 00:14:56.291
I have finally perceived
the poetry and the beauty of it all.

178
00:14:56.875 --> 00:14:58.416
<i>Of Candela.</i>

179
00:14:58.916 --> 00:15:01.833
<i>Nobody has fed me since I was 5 years old.</i>

180
00:15:06.125 --> 00:15:09.833
<i>When my mother would play that game</i>
<i>of "open up. here comes the plane."</i>

181
00:15:09.916 --> 00:15:11.583
<i>I would get anxious.</i>

182
00:15:12.083 --> 00:15:15.500
<i>And yet. with Candela…</i>
<i>everything tasted glorious.</i>

183
00:15:15.583 --> 00:15:19.083
But that's not all.

184
00:15:19.166 --> 00:15:21.291
After dinner. we went out for a walk…

185
00:15:21.375 --> 00:15:22.666
with a bunny rabbit.

186
00:15:23.625 --> 00:15:24.625
The furry kind.

187
00:15:26.791 --> 00:15:28.166
Magical.

188
00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:32.875
And I was enchanted. Its name is Pomelo.

189
00:15:33.666 --> 00:15:36.208
Isn't that hilarious?

190
00:15:36.291 --> 00:15:37.791
You wanna know something else?

191
00:15:37.875 --> 00:15:40.375
She takes her bunny
for a morning stroll. every morning.

192
00:15:40.458 --> 00:15:45.625
<i>On a leash. like it's a German Shepherd.</i>
<i>to soak up the sun's energy.</i>

193
00:15:46.125 --> 00:15:49.166
<i>Personally. I have never been</i>
<i>a great lover of animals.</i>

194
00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.541
<i>Especially not rodents.</i>

195
00:15:50.625 --> 00:15:54.250
<i>However… there I was.</i>
<i>playing in the grass.</i>

196
00:15:54.333 --> 00:15:56.000
<i>bonding with a bunny.</i>

197
00:15:56.750 --> 00:16:00.458
Everything that I believed
to be vulgar before…

198
00:16:00.541 --> 00:16:03.291
Well. now I feel a magnetic attraction.

199
00:16:03.375 --> 00:16:07.125
What I once thought to be obnoxious
and ostentatious.

200
00:16:07.208 --> 00:16:09.125
in fact. turned out to be a hymn to life.

201
00:16:12.083 --> 00:16:14.500
No more shrinking from life.

202
00:16:14.583 --> 00:16:18.291
We must live…
our lives fully and completely to exist!

203
00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.875
And play with rabbits.

204
00:16:24.333 --> 00:16:25.958
I wanted to share this news with you.

205
00:16:26.041 --> 00:16:29.041
in case you might be worried about
who I fall in love with for our new job.

206
00:16:29.125 --> 00:16:31.875
This is nothing
like what happened in Paris.

207
00:16:31.958 --> 00:16:34.708
And has nothing…
to do with the duchess's treasure.

208
00:16:36.791 --> 00:16:39.125
Well. I'm going to use this fork. Mm?

209
00:16:39.958 --> 00:16:44.000
You know. just in case you get excited.
watching me eating my food.

210
00:16:44.083 --> 00:16:45.166
Mm.

211
00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:48.416
It's true.
Quite often. opposites attract. Right?

212
00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:53.833
- I'm just wondering how you got shot.
- Does it involve a bed and a boyfriend?

213
00:16:53.916 --> 00:16:55.791
No. there is no boyfriend.

214
00:16:55.875 --> 00:16:58.041
And there is no bed.
And no kissing either.

215
00:16:58.125 --> 00:17:00.916
There was absolutely
nothing inappropriate between us.

216
00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.541
I earned these bullet holes

217
00:17:02.625 --> 00:17:05.625
simply because she caught me
foraging in her house.

218
00:17:07.041 --> 00:17:09.625
And so. to celebrate this new philosophy.

219
00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:14.250
we… we're gonna spend
the rest of our day exploring.

220
00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:48.916
The Land Registry indicates that
the estate is made up of 8.300 hectares.

221
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.416
And that's the only info I got.

222
00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:53.250
Google Earth doesn't even show images
from inside.

223
00:17:53.333 --> 00:17:55.166
It's like it's a ghost estate.

224
00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:57.333
There are a few photos of the winery.

225
00:17:57.416 --> 00:17:59.000
They date back to the '60s.

226
00:17:59.083 --> 00:18:02.708
It was a building with a large glass dome
in the middle of the countryside.

227
00:18:02.791 --> 00:18:05.750
There was an underground cellar
used for fermenting the wines.

228
00:18:05.833 --> 00:18:07.750
But the building was demolished years ago.

229
00:18:07.833 --> 00:18:09.791
Shortly after he built that train line.

230
00:18:09.875 --> 00:18:11.625
We have to find that wine cellar.

231
00:18:11.708 --> 00:18:14.166
How do we do that?
Are we supposed to jump the fence?

232
00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.541
We do it
with the newest member of the team.

233
00:18:17.791 --> 00:18:19.833
The imperial Iberian eagle.

234
00:18:19.916 --> 00:18:21.708
Today we'll just do a flyover.

235
00:18:24.625 --> 00:18:26.041
Let's do this.

236
00:18:26.791 --> 00:18:28.666
Up. up. and away.

237
00:18:33.666 --> 00:18:35.666
Keila. head west. please.

238
00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:39.291
Once we locate the family home.
we'll be able to find our bearings.

239
00:18:46.166 --> 00:18:47.250
What's that?

240
00:18:47.958 --> 00:18:49.000
Keila. zoom in.

241
00:18:51.416 --> 00:18:54.750
{\an8}Dead animals. And lots of them.

242
00:18:56.333 --> 00:18:58.000
{\an8}There's an electric fence.

243
00:19:00.208 --> 00:19:03.958
It would appear this one has
much higher voltage than usual fences.

244
00:19:04.041 --> 00:19:07.125
{\an8}Current above 30 milliamps
is enough to cause a heart attack.

245
00:19:11.625 --> 00:19:13.791
Look. There's something
behind those olive trees there.

246
00:19:15.375 --> 00:19:18.291
{\an8}That's the family home.
Cameron. find it on the map.

247
00:19:23.291 --> 00:19:26.291
You gotta be kidding.
He has his own bullring?

248
00:19:26.375 --> 00:19:29.166
Get closer. Let's see how His Highness
keeps himself entertained.

249
00:19:36.208 --> 00:19:37.458
Zoom in all the way.

250
00:19:44.083 --> 00:19:47.791
{\an8}- Pull back.
- It looks like the train leaves from here.

251
00:19:47.875 --> 00:19:51.458
{\an8}So the wine cellar must be
within a one-kilometer radius at most.

252
00:19:51.541 --> 00:19:54.833
And somewhere within that area.
there's an air vent.

253
00:19:54.916 --> 00:19:57.541
Every underground construction.
by law. has to have a vent.

254
00:19:57.625 --> 00:19:59.458
So if we can locate it.
then theoretically.

255
00:19:59.541 --> 00:20:02.958
all we have to do is draw
a straight line from it to the home.

256
00:20:03.041 --> 00:20:04.458
Then we'll find the cellar.

257
00:20:09.958 --> 00:20:11.458
{\an8}Wait. Stop there.

258
00:20:11.541 --> 00:20:12.791
Zoom in.

259
00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:19.958
The ventilation shaft.

260
00:20:20.041 --> 00:20:21.833
Cameron. get the coordinates.

261
00:20:21.916 --> 00:20:26.125
Draw a line from the house to the vent…
and keep going.

262
00:20:36.541 --> 00:20:39.208
It seems to be the same glass dome
from the old building.

263
00:20:39.291 --> 00:20:41.041
Minus the building.

264
00:20:48.625 --> 00:20:51.375
{\an8}Who would hide their treasure
under a glass dome?

265
00:20:51.458 --> 00:20:54.083
That would be someone
with a passion for art and for poetry

266
00:20:54.166 --> 00:20:55.458
who knows that some things

267
00:20:55.541 --> 00:20:57.833
are best appreciated
only in natural light.

268
00:20:58.583 --> 00:21:02.583
{\an8}Such as… rare sapphires
or a giant blue diamond.

269
00:21:02.666 --> 00:21:07.416
Or… just maybe.
a stupendous. wonderful work of art.

270
00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:11.125
Don't you feel that insatiable desire
to discover what's hidden down there?

271
00:21:15.875 --> 00:21:17.250
- What's happening?
- I don't know.

272
00:21:17.333 --> 00:21:19.041
It's not responding to my commands.

273
00:21:19.125 --> 00:21:21.041
We're losing altitude. It's dropping fast.

274
00:21:21.125 --> 00:21:22.916
It's gone rogue.

275
00:21:23.916 --> 00:21:25.250
The connection is unstable.

276
00:21:27.208 --> 00:21:29.750
- What's going on?
- I'm not sure. but we've gone blind.

277
00:21:33.041 --> 00:21:35.958
Sixty meters and falling.
They most likely have jammers.

278
00:21:38.416 --> 00:21:41.750
The drone frequency is high.
but it doesn't seem to be enough.

279
00:21:41.833 --> 00:21:43.875
- Keila. bring it in now!
- Thirty meters…

280
00:21:43.958 --> 00:21:45.708
- I'm doing what I can.
- Twenty meters…

281
00:21:45.791 --> 00:21:48.166
The GPS is working.
The drone isn't that far from us.

282
00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:51.166
- It's nosediving.
- Ten meters…

283
00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:54.083
Keila. it's almost on the ground.
Try to make it land.

284
00:22:02.625 --> 00:22:04.166
The eagle's down.

285
00:22:05.958 --> 00:22:06.833
Do you hear that?

286
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.000
Turn up the volume.

287
00:22:16.833 --> 00:22:18.750
It's the fucking cattle.

288
00:22:18.833 --> 00:22:21.125
They're scratching and sniffing the drone.

289
00:22:25.583 --> 00:22:28.500
- We need to get it back immediately.
- No.

290
00:22:29.375 --> 00:22:31.875
Going inside that place
without a plan would be suicide.

291
00:22:31.958 --> 00:22:34.041
And I'm not talking
about the electric fences.

292
00:22:34.125 --> 00:22:36.666
This duke isn't
your typical entitled nobleman.

293
00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:37.708
He's a criminal!

294
00:22:37.791 --> 00:22:38.916
Precisely.

295
00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:41.958
So what do you think he'll do
when he finds a drone on his property?

296
00:22:42.041 --> 00:22:42.916
Oh! Wait…

297
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:46.333
Maybe this cute drone belongs to the guy
who's interested in my art collection

298
00:22:46.416 --> 00:22:48.416
and who also has a gang of thieves!

299
00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:54.375
If that happens. him going to the police
will be the least of our worries.

300
00:22:55.458 --> 00:22:57.458
Because his only other option is murder.

301
00:22:58.666 --> 00:22:59.791
I'll go get it.

302
00:23:02.416 --> 00:23:05.291
I'm sure I can locate it pretty fast
using the GPS coordinates.

303
00:23:05.375 --> 00:23:07.625
No. no. no. no. Keila. no.

304
00:23:07.708 --> 00:23:09.541
If you go. I'm going with you.

305
00:23:10.041 --> 00:23:13.375
That was a sophisticated drone.
yet they managed to jam it.

306
00:23:13.458 --> 00:23:16.166
So your earpieces
most likely won't function.

307
00:23:18.583 --> 00:23:20.250
Out there. you'll be on your own.

308
00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:29.500
We'll keep a close eye on you.

309
00:23:29.583 --> 00:23:32.166
If you see anything unusual.
don't take any risks.

310
00:23:32.250 --> 00:23:34.125
You immediately turn back.

311
00:23:52.541 --> 00:23:53.625
Over there.

312
00:24:33.458 --> 00:24:35.750
Careful. Slowly.

313
00:24:57.166 --> 00:24:58.541
Can either one of you tell me

314
00:24:58.625 --> 00:25:01.583
why I agreed
that Keila would go fetch the lost drone?

315
00:25:01.666 --> 00:25:05.666
I mean. obviously she's the one
with the most brains here.

316
00:25:07.458 --> 00:25:11.833
Because if I sent you or him.
chances are that sooner or later.

317
00:25:11.916 --> 00:25:15.583
both of you
will tear each other to pieces.

318
00:25:15.666 --> 00:25:17.083
Ever since you got here.

319
00:25:17.166 --> 00:25:20.000
it's been nothing but long faces
and insults…

320
00:25:20.083 --> 00:25:24.166
What makes you think any of us want
to listen and put up with your bullshit?

321
00:25:27.791 --> 00:25:30.041
It's obvious you've broken the rules.

322
00:25:30.125 --> 00:25:33.708
Sure. but to be fair.
Bruce and Keila broke them too.

323
00:25:33.791 --> 00:25:36.125
No. they've managed to stay content.

324
00:25:38.041 --> 00:25:40.916
So. I am going to ask you two
two questions.

325
00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:43.375
Firstly. do you want to remain
in this gang?

326
00:25:46.083 --> 00:25:47.708
Please answer me now.

327
00:25:47.791 --> 00:25:49.166
Yes.

328
00:25:49.250 --> 00:25:50.541
Yes.

329
00:25:50.625 --> 00:25:52.750
Good. And for my second question.

330
00:25:52.833 --> 00:25:56.916
Imagine if you had to infiltrate
something like a train.

331
00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:58.875
Yeah. Like the Orient Express.
for example.

332
00:25:58.958 --> 00:26:01.875
And then. imagine that you had
to pretend to be a couple

333
00:26:01.958 --> 00:26:05.125
and spend the night together
in the same bed.

334
00:26:06.125 --> 00:26:07.875
Would you do it?

335
00:26:09.791 --> 00:26:11.833
Yes.

336
00:26:15.916 --> 00:26:16.916
No.

337
00:26:20.833 --> 00:26:23.125
I don't know what happened between you.

338
00:26:23.208 --> 00:26:26.541
But what I do know
is that both of you are 25 years old.

339
00:26:26.625 --> 00:26:28.875
you have four million euros each.

340
00:26:28.958 --> 00:26:32.125
you're beautiful.
healthy. and full of energy…

341
00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:36.083
And even though you have it all.
you managed to screw it up!

342
00:26:46.708 --> 00:26:48.708
- Over there. you see it?
- Yeah.

343
00:26:53.500 --> 00:26:55.625
Bruce…

344
00:26:55.708 --> 00:26:58.041
Okay. listen to me.
You sprained your ankle. and it's bad.

345
00:26:58.125 --> 00:26:59.916
- It really hurts.
- Hide it.

346
00:27:20.583 --> 00:27:23.333
- This is private property.
- I'm really sorry.

347
00:27:23.416 --> 00:27:25.375
We came here to photograph the bulls.

348
00:27:25.458 --> 00:27:27.416
and my girlfriend fell
and sprained her ankle.

349
00:27:35.875 --> 00:27:37.958
You need to be careful where you walk.

350
00:27:38.041 --> 00:27:39.416
It can be dangerous.

351
00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:41.125
I guess you didn't see

352
00:27:41.208 --> 00:27:43.833
all the no trespassing signs
around the property?

353
00:27:43.916 --> 00:27:48.375
If I see anything moving here…
I pull out my weapon. and I shoot to kill.

354
00:27:53.750 --> 00:27:55.083
You wanted to see the bulls?

355
00:27:55.166 --> 00:27:58.125
Yeah. to take some photos
in their habitat.

356
00:27:59.625 --> 00:28:01.208
Perfect. Let me show you.

357
00:28:01.791 --> 00:28:03.291
I feed them every day.

358
00:28:27.958 --> 00:28:30.000
Now's the time to take those photos.

359
00:28:30.500 --> 00:28:33.708
No longer up to it. I guess?

360
00:28:40.833 --> 00:28:44.958
C'mon. Sit down over there.
Let me take a look at your ankle.

361
00:28:45.958 --> 00:28:47.958
I've seen lots of sprains out hunting.

362
00:28:49.416 --> 00:28:50.541
Sit down.

363
00:28:52.166 --> 00:28:53.416
Let me see.

364
00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:57.333
Gotta check for swelling.

365
00:29:10.208 --> 00:29:13.541
- Does it hurt?
- Yes. A bit. yeah.

366
00:29:14.750 --> 00:29:15.750
How much is a bit?

367
00:29:16.750 --> 00:29:19.125
It's painful when I walk.

368
00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:25.666
I'm sorry. but it looks. um… pretty bad.

369
00:29:29.916 --> 00:29:31.916
It's quite a serious sprain.

370
00:29:34.500 --> 00:29:37.541
Lucky for you. I have what it takes.

371
00:29:41.583 --> 00:29:45.833
This is what I do to help… all my bitches.

372
00:29:55.166 --> 00:29:56.375
Gently rubbing this in

373
00:29:58.166 --> 00:29:59.958
helps relieve the swelling.

374
00:30:08.208 --> 00:30:10.500
It's okay. kid. pull out your phone.

375
00:30:12.166 --> 00:30:13.750
See if there's any signal.

376
00:30:14.916 --> 00:30:16.083
C'mon.

377
00:30:16.833 --> 00:30:18.125
Make your call!

378
00:30:18.708 --> 00:30:20.291
Fuckin' do it!

379
00:30:25.541 --> 00:30:27.416
No signal.

380
00:30:28.583 --> 00:30:30.541
This entire area is off-grid.

381
00:30:34.125 --> 00:30:35.916
Let's get you some help. C'mon.

382
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:38.083
No. there's really no need.
It's much better.

383
00:30:38.166 --> 00:30:40.166
- No. no. c'mon. Let's go.
- I can walk now.

384
00:30:40.250 --> 00:30:42.916
It's all good. man. I got this. okay?
Hey. I'll take care of her now.

385
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:43.875
Thank you so much.

386
00:30:43.958 --> 00:30:46.708
Look. you see. I can just carry her
on my back. It's easy.

387
00:30:46.791 --> 00:30:49.166
Then you must be stupid. kid.

388
00:30:50.208 --> 00:30:52.041
How are you gonna carry her?

389
00:30:53.583 --> 00:30:55.083
Shh!

390
00:30:58.083 --> 00:31:01.916
Are you gonna jump the electric fence?
And the wall?

391
00:31:03.791 --> 00:31:05.583
Easy. girls!

392
00:31:06.875 --> 00:31:08.458
Get inside.

393
00:31:09.375 --> 00:31:10.583
Go on. Inside.

394
00:31:15.083 --> 00:31:17.208
And you… in the back.

395
00:31:20.958 --> 00:31:23.166
Forget it. No way.
Keila. get out of there.

396
00:31:23.250 --> 00:31:24.833
C'mon. open the door.

397
00:31:24.916 --> 00:31:26.666
Open the door! The door. Keila!

398
00:31:26.750 --> 00:31:29.250
- You need a key to open it.
- Open the door!

399
00:31:30.208 --> 00:31:31.625
Please. sir.

400
00:31:32.416 --> 00:31:34.458
Open the damn door!

401
00:31:35.458 --> 00:31:37.875
Please let me out! Bruce!

402
00:31:45.916 --> 00:31:46.916
Open it!

403
00:31:47.666 --> 00:31:50.125
I help you.
and now you're giving me this shit?

404
00:31:50.625 --> 00:31:53.500
Step away from the truck. right now. Easy.

405
00:31:54.250 --> 00:31:55.541
Keep movin'.

406
00:31:56.125 --> 00:31:57.916
Now turn around.

407
00:31:58.583 --> 00:32:00.583
Bruce!

408
00:32:00.666 --> 00:32:02.833
Keep walking. asshole.

409
00:32:15.416 --> 00:32:17.208
Tell me what you're doing here.

410
00:32:17.291 --> 00:32:19.750
One or two injured trespassers.
it's all the same to me.

411
00:32:21.333 --> 00:32:22.875
Enough of this shit.

412
00:32:22.958 --> 00:32:24.208
Keep walking.

413
00:32:25.083 --> 00:32:28.208
- I said keep walking.
- Fine.

414
00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:31.583
We broke in. Happy?

415
00:32:31.666 --> 00:32:33.875
And now we'll leave like nothing happened.

416
00:32:35.666 --> 00:32:37.708
- Let me get her.
- Don't fucking move!

417
00:32:38.583 --> 00:32:40.666
One more step. and I'll shoot you.

418
00:32:41.250 --> 00:32:42.750
Go on. Pull the trigger.

419
00:32:43.541 --> 00:32:46.125
But you better not miss. man.
'Cause I'll smash your head in.

420
00:32:46.208 --> 00:32:47.416
Oh. yeah?

421
00:32:59.833 --> 00:33:01.916
Next shot. I'll blow your brains out.

422
00:33:03.208 --> 00:33:06.083
So. kid… why are you here? Tell me now.

423
00:33:07.333 --> 00:33:09.833
We're trying to locate the vent
to the duke's underground cellar.

424
00:33:31.125 --> 00:33:33.583
Don't move! Or I'll shoot.

425
00:33:51.541 --> 00:33:54.041
- We need to bring him with us.
- What are you saying?

426
00:33:54.125 --> 00:33:56.708
- We have to go. get out of here!
- Calm down. Relax. calm down!

427
00:33:56.791 --> 00:33:58.708
We have to.
If he dies. that makes me a murderer.

428
00:33:58.791 --> 00:34:01.708
And if he actually survives.
he knows exactly why we're here.

429
00:34:01.791 --> 00:34:03.041
But how would he know?

430
00:34:03.125 --> 00:34:04.458
Because I told him.

431
00:34:05.833 --> 00:34:06.958
Let's go.

432
00:34:15.333 --> 00:34:17.375
How are we gonna get outta here?

433
00:34:17.875 --> 00:34:21.125
- We'll have to carry him out.
- And how do we get him over the main gate?

434
00:36:02.166 --> 00:36:03.916
Is he humming a tune?

435
00:36:05.541 --> 00:36:07.416
Or does he have something to tell us?

436
00:36:21.083 --> 00:36:23.000
Roi. see if he has a phone.

437
00:36:33.875 --> 00:36:35.833
Well. he doesn't seem to have any friends.

438
00:36:35.916 --> 00:36:39.500
There are no missed calls.
no new messages.

439
00:36:40.583 --> 00:36:43.250
There are a few hours left before dawn.

440
00:36:43.333 --> 00:36:46.166
But when morning comes.
we have to let the creep go.

441
00:36:46.250 --> 00:36:48.000
and we need to get out of Seville.

442
00:36:48.083 --> 00:36:50.041
So. where does that leave us?

443
00:36:52.458 --> 00:36:54.541
Well. that means we have an opportunity.

444
00:36:55.250 --> 00:36:57.583
We have an opportunity for what?

445
00:37:01.583 --> 00:37:05.333
An opportunity
to pull off the robbery tonight.

446
00:37:06.305 --> 00:38:06.909
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-
